{
 "sankey": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Where FY2027&rsquo;s $450.7 million comes from, and where it goes</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">General Fund sources and uses, the FY2027 budget adopted by Town Meeting in May 2026, with the override</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"sankey-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Diagram of the FY2027 General Fund, $450.7 million, as adopted with the override. Sources: property tax $323.9 million (72%), local receipts $37.6 million, debt exclusion $35.4 million, state aid $26.7 million, free cash $18.3 million and other funds $8.8 million. Uses: schools $149.8 million (33%), Town departments $103.5 million, employee benefits $99.1 million, other non-departmental $48.8 million, debt exclusion debt service $35.4 million and other debt service $14.0 million.\" id=\"sankey-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 500\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"sankey-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"sankey-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"sankey-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "funds-sankey": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Brookline&rsquo;s full financial picture: where every dollar comes from, which fund it sits in, and what it pays for</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">FY2027. Sources &rarr; fund &rarr; uses, all five funds at once. Note how little crosses between funds, and that what does cross runs <em>from</em> the enterprise funds <em>to</em> the General Fund, not the other way. Debt exclusion is shown in its own color: it is property tax, but restricted by law to the specific bonds voters approved. The General Fund is the budget Town Meeting adopted in May 2026, with the override; the other funds are from the FY2027 Financial Plan. CPA is the Financial Plan&rsquo;s one gap: it isn&rsquo;t budgeted there at all, so it is shown at its FY2024 audited actual.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"funds-sankey-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Diagram of all five Town funds in FY2027, about $495 million in total. The General Fund is about $447 million, 90% of the total; Water and Sewer is about $35.6 million; Recreation, Golf and Community Preservation are $3 million to $6 million each. Little money moves between funds, and what does moves from the enterprise funds to the General Fund, about $4.0 million to pay employee benefits.\" id=\"funds-sankey-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 860\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"funds-sankey-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"note\" style=\"margin:14px 0 0;font-size:12.5px\">\n        <b>Two adjustments, so every dollar is counted once.</b> (1) The <b>$4,019,498</b> that Water&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Sewer, Recreation and Golf reimburse the General Fund for their staff&rsquo;s fringe benefits is drawn as its own band from each fund to Employee&nbsp;Benefits, what it actually pays for, and so is removed from the General Fund&rsquo;s &ldquo;Other Available Funds,&rdquo; where the budget books it. (2) The General Fund&rsquo;s own Recreation Department (<b>$1,258,275</b>) is split out of Town&nbsp;Departments and drawn into the shared <b>Recreation programs</b> node, which is where the tax subsidy of recreation becomes visible. Employee&nbsp;Benefits still totals $99.1M and Recreation programs $6.3M; only the question of <em>who funds them</em> is made explicit.\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"funds-sankey-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"funds-sankey-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "line": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Two decades of diverging growth rates</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Indexed to FY2005 = 100. Solid lines: the whole budget, both sides. Dashed lines: three levy-limit-only counterfactuals, all excluding debt exclusion; see the note below.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-row\">\n        <div class=\"chart-col\">\n          <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"line-wrap\">\n            <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Line chart, FY2005 to FY2025, indexed to FY2005 equals 100. By FY2025 employee benefits reached 293, schools 242 and total spending 216, while total revenue reached 232. The levy limit reached 248 with overrides, 215 without them, and 164 with only the automatic 2.5% a year.\" id=\"line-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 500\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n            <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"line-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"legend legend-vertical\" id=\"line-legend\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"line-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"line-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "waterfall": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Where the $175 million in FY2005&rarr;FY2025 property tax growth actually came from</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Same three counterfactuals as the chart above, restacked as cumulative dollars instead of indexed lines. Scoped to FY2005&ndash;2025, same as everything else on this page.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-row\">\n        <div class=\"chart-col\">\n          <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"waterfall-wrap\">\n            <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stacked area chart of Brookline&#x27;s property tax levy limit, FY2005 to FY2025, excluding debt exclusions. It grew from $118.2 million to $293.1 million. Of the $175 million increase, the automatic 2.5% a year added $75.5 million (43%), new growth from construction and renovation $60.7 million (35%), and the four overrides $38.7 million (22%).\" id=\"waterfall-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 650 480\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n            <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"waterfall-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"waterfall-stats\">\n          <div class=\"wf-stat total\" data-layer=\"top\">\n            <span class=\"wf-val\">$293.1M</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-pct\">FY2025 total</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-label\">Property tax levy limit (excludes debt exclusion)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"wf-stat\" data-layer=\"overrides\" style=\"border-top-color: var(--copper)\">\n            <span class=\"wf-val\">$38.7M</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-pct\">22% of the $175M growth</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-label\">Overrides (FY2009, FY2016, FY2019, FY2024, compounded to FY2025)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"wf-stat\" data-layer=\"newgrowth\" style=\"border-top-color: var(--line-benefits)\">\n            <span class=\"wf-val\">$60.7M</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-pct\">35% of the $175M growth</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-label\">New growth (construction + renovation)</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"wf-stat\" data-layer=\"pct25\" style=\"border-top-color: var(--pine)\">\n            <span class=\"wf-val\">$75.5M</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-pct\">43% of the $175M growth</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-label\">2.5%/yr automatic growth</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"wf-stat\" data-layer=\"base\" style=\"border-top-color: var(--wf-base)\">\n            <span class=\"wf-val\">$118.2M</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-pct\">FY2005 starting point</span>\n            <span class=\"wf-label\">Property that already existed in FY2005</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"waterfall-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"waterfall-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "expense-growth": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Where expense growth actually came from, FY2005 &rarr; FY2025</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Each band is one category, same order both years. Height = dollar size; the label is that category&rsquo;s 20-year CAGR. Debt service is split into the part inside the levy limit and the part funded by voter-approved exclusions, which carries its own matching revenue.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"expense-growth-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Diagram comparing annual General Fund spending by category in FY2005, $169.0 million, and FY2025, $364.7 million. Education grew from $60.4 million to $146.4 million (4.5% a year), benefits and fixed costs from $30.5 million to $89.4 million (5.5% a year), public safety from $25.4 million to $43.5 million (2.7% a year), and debt service paid by debt exclusions from $1.7 million to $22.0 million. The other categories grew between 0.5% and 2.7% a year.\" id=\"expense-growth-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1060 620\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"expense-growth-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"expense-growth-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"expense-growth-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "liabilities": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Two unfunded liabilities, neither one a straight line</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Net pension liability (Town&rsquo;s ~96&ndash;97% share) and net OPEB liability, by year</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"liab-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Line chart of two unfunded liabilities. The Town&#x27;s share of the net pension liability went from $184 million in 2014 to a high of $240 million in 2018, fell to $125 million in 2021 and was $171 million in 2023. The net retiree health (OPEB) liability went from $254 million in 2017 to $190 million in 2023 and $201 million in 2024.\" id=\"liab-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 420\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"liab-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"liab-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"liab-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"liab-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "control": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Growth of what Brookline controls, and what it does not</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Indexed to FY2005 = 100. Solid lines are revenue Brookline sets for itself; dashed lines are set by the Legislature. Both are measured against operating expenditure, in black. The top line is what the levy limit actually did, 2.5% plus new growth plus the four overrides in this window. Debt exclusions are excluded throughout, on both sides.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"control-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Line chart, FY2005 to FY2025, indexed to FY2005 equals 100, comparing revenue with operating spending, which reached 205. Revenue Brookline sets for itself: the levy limit with overrides reached 248, without overrides 215, and fees the Town sets 199. Revenue set by the Legislature: the levy limit with only the automatic 2.5% reached 164, and state aid 148.\" id=\"control-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 460\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"control-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"control-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"control-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "unit-breakeven": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>When a home covers its costs</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Children per home at which a home&rsquo;s property tax just covers the Town services and schooling it adds, by assessed value. Below a line the home pays its way; above it, it does not. The dotted green line is an owner-occupied home, taxed on its value less the residential exemption ($354,974 in FY2026).</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"unitbe-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Line chart of the school-age children per home at which a new home&#x27;s property tax covers its costs, by assessed value, in FY2027 and FY2040. In FY2027 a $425,000 home breaks even at about 0.21 children, an $800,000 home at about 0.44 and a $1.2 million home at about 0.68. By FY2040 the same homes break even at about 0.16, 0.35 and 0.54. An owner-occupied home pays tax on its value less the residential exemption, $354,974, so its line sits further right: in FY2027 an owner-occupied $800,000 home breaks even at about 0.22 children and a $1.2 million home at about 0.46. The forecast averages 0.244 children per new home; ten recent Brookline buildings range from 0.03 to 0.56. An average single-family home, assessed at $2.78 million, breaks even at about 1.6 children.\" id=\"unitbe-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 500\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"unitbe-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"unitbe-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"unitbe-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"unitbe-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "decisions": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>What decides the 2040 budget</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Change in the FY2040 annual balance when one assumption moves from the base case, $ millions a year. The base case leaves $11.5 million of room in FY2040.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"decisions-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Horizontal bar chart of how much each change, one at a time, moves the FY2040 balance from the base case, with a dashed line at the base case&#x27;s whole FY2040 room. Bars are grouped by who decides: Brookline, growth, or mostly outside Brookline. The data table below the chart lists every value.\" id=\"decisions-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 430\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"decisions-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"decisions-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"decisions-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"decisions-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "growth-paths": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Room in the budget at four new-growth rates</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Revenue minus annual General Fund spending, $ millions a year, with the added or missing growth in today&rsquo;s mix. Everything else is the base case.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gpaths-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" id=\"gpaths-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 440\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gpaths-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gpaths-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gpaths-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gpaths-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "growth-mix": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Same added tax, different costs</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">New growth 0.8 point above the trend (the 80th-percentile rate, 2.03%), by where it comes from: added tax and added costs in FY2040, $ millions a year.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gmix-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" id=\"gmix-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 300\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gmix-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gmix-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gmix-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gmix-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "enroll-seats": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Enrollment is falling below what the schools are staffed for</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Public school students, PK&ndash;12. Actual through FY2026, then NESDEC&rsquo;s projection updated for actual births (the base case) and, dashed through FY2034, the School Department&rsquo;s forecast and NESDEC&rsquo;s forecast as published, before the births update (both scaled to this fall&rsquo;s count). The shaded area is the empty seats if classes stay at the FY2027 level, as the base case assumes.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"seats-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Line chart of public school enrollment, FY2010 to FY2040. Enrollment peaked at 7,855 in FY2019 and is 6,833 in FY2027, the level the schools are staffed for. The base case projection falls to about 5,400 by FY2040, leaving a growing area of empty seats. The School Department&#x27;s forecast instead rises to about 7,400 by FY2034; NESDEC&#x27;s forecast as published falls to about 6,230.\" id=\"seats-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 400\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"seats-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"seats-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"seats-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"seats-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "housing-fill": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>What extra homes add to the 2040 budget, after their costs</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Extra homes beyond the base case, built by FY2040. Each bar is the added property tax and other revenue minus the added Town and school costs, in FY2040, $ millions a year.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"hfill-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of what extra homes add to the FY2040 budget after their costs. About 2,100 extra homes leave the budget $1.2 million a year worse off under the usual estimate, and add $8.2 million a year if their children fill empty seats. About 5,100, roughly what the empty seats hold, add $4.2 million and $16.7 million.\" id=\"hfill-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 340\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"hfill-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"hfill-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"hfill-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"hfill-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "seats-homes": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>How many new homes in total before the open seats are full</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">New homes from FY2028. The gray area is the base case&rsquo;s own new homes, already counted in the enrollment forecast. Each line adds the homes whose children would fill the seats that open as enrollment falls below the FY2027 level, at three rates of school-age children per home.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"shomes-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" id=\"shomes-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 400\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"shomes-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"shomes-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"shomes-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"shomes-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "home-net": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>What a new home brings the Town each year, after its costs</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Property tax minus Town services and schools, per home per year, at the forecast&rsquo;s 0.244 school-age children per home. Two bars per home: the usual estimate, and children filling empty seats.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"hnet-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of what each type of new home brings the Town each year after its costs, at 0.244 school-age children per home, two ways. Under the usual estimate, with new staff for every student: a $434,000 apartment in a large building, minus $527; the typical $585,000 new home, plus $1,016; a $673,000 apartment in a small building, plus $1,916; the average new-construction project at $794,000, plus $3,160; a $1.18 million condominium, plus $7,068. If the children fill empty seats, the same homes bring plus $2,977, $4,520, $5,420, $6,664 and $10,572.\" id=\"hnet-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 370\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"hnet-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"hnet-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"hnet-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"hnet-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "outlook": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>The outlook: revenue minus spending each year</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Base case, $ millions a year, FY2026 to FY2040. The dashed line takes out the May 2026 override&rsquo;s revenue.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"outlook-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"outlook-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"outlook-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"outlook-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"outlook-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"outlook-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "decide": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>What drives the 2040 budget</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">How much each assumption, moved from the base case, changes revenue minus spending in a single year: FY2040 (left) and FY2035 (right), on the same scale. Colors show who decides.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"decide-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"decide-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 650\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"decide-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"decide-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"decide-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"decide-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "causes": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Where the $177 million went, FY2011 to FY2025</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">The increase in annual General Fund spending from FY2011 to FY2025, by cause. Colors show who sets each cause. Hover a bar for its pieces.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"causes-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"causes-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 330\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"causes-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"causes-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"causes-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"causes-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "staff-enroll": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>School staff and enrollment</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Indexed to FY2011 = 100. Staff are full-time equivalents; data begin FY2008.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"staffenroll-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"staffenroll-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 360\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"staffenroll-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"staffenroll-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"staffenroll-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"staffenroll-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "tax-bill": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>A typical tax bill to FY2040</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">The Town&rsquo;s FY2026 median bill, owner-occupied (with the residential exemption), or the average rental apartment&rsquo;s (no exemption), for a home whose value moves with the town average. Every type of home is assumed to gain value at the same rate. Four paths; the base case assumes no further votes. The legend gives each path&rsquo;s average growth a year, FY2026&ndash;40.</p>\n      </div>\n      <p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-size:14px\"><label for=\"taxbill-home\">Home: </label>\n        <select id=\"taxbill-home\"><option value=\"single_family\">Single-family</option><option value=\"two_family\">Two-family</option><option value=\"condo\">Condominium</option><option value=\"apartment\">Rental apartment (average per unit)</option></select></p>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"taxbill-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"taxbill-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"taxbill-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"taxbill-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"taxbill-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"taxbill-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "bill-calc": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Your bill</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Enter your home&rsquo;s FY2026 assessed value, or your FY2026 tax bill. Nothing you enter leaves this page.</p>\n      </div>\n      <fieldset style=\"border:0;padding:0;margin:12px 0 0;font-size:15px\">\n        <legend class=\"sr-only\" style=\"position:absolute;left:-9999px\">Start from</legend>\n        <label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"billcalc-mode\" value=\"value\" checked> My assessed value</label>\n        &nbsp;&nbsp;<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"billcalc-mode\" value=\"bill\"> My FY2026 bill</label>\n      </fieldset>\n      <div id=\"billcalc-by-value\" style=\"margin-top:10px;font-size:15px\">\n        <label for=\"billcalc-value\">FY2026 assessed value ($)</label>\n        <input id=\"billcalc-value\" inputmode=\"decimal\" style=\"width:11em;margin:0 12px 0 6px\">\n        <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"billcalc-owner\" checked> I live there (residential exemption)</label>\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"billcalc-by-bill\" hidden style=\"margin-top:10px;font-size:15px\">\n        <label for=\"billcalc-bill\">FY2026 tax bill ($)</label>\n        <input id=\"billcalc-bill\" inputmode=\"decimal\" style=\"width:11em;margin-left:6px\">\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"billcalc-out\" aria-live=\"polite\" style=\"margin-top:14px;font-size:15px\"></div>\n      <div id=\"billcalc-chart\" hidden>\n        <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"billcalc-wrap\">\n          <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"billcalc-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n          <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"billcalc-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"legend\" id=\"billcalc-legend\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>",
 "who-sets": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Who sets the $177 million</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">The same increase in annual General Fund spending, FY2011 to FY2025, grouped by who controls each cause. Hover a bar for what it includes.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"whosets-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"whosets-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 220\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"whosets-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"whosets-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"whosets-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "enroll-assume": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>The forecasts' two key assumptions</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Left: births to Brookline residents, actual and as each forecast assumes (Cropper-McKibben publishes five-year totals, shown as yearly averages). Right: students per birth, enrollment divided by the births of the 13 years whose children are in K-12; for each forecast, measured against its own births, so it shows what the forecast assumes about families moving in. Fiscal years on the right.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"eassume-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"eassume-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 400\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"eassume-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"eassume-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"eassume-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "births-towns": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Births have fallen across the region, fastest in the inner suburbs</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Births to residents, each group's 2005–09 average = 100. Neighboring cities and inner suburbs: Cambridge, Somerville, Newton, Watertown, Arlington, Belmont. Family suburbs: Lexington, Wellesley, Needham, Winchester, Concord, Wayland, Sudbury, Weston. Source: Department of Public Health birth reports.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"birthstowns-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"birthstowns-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 360\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"birthstowns-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"birthstowns-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"birthstowns-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "kpb-housing": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Towns with more family-sized homes draw more kindergartners per birth</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Each dot is a town. Kindergartners per birth: fall 2025 kindergarten divided by resident births in 2020, the year most of the class was born; above 1 (dashed line), more young families arrive than leave. Family-sized: houses and condos with 6 or more rooms, from each town's assessment records. Sources: DESE, Department of Public Health, MassGIS.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"kpbhousing-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"kpbhousing-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 420\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"kpbhousing-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"kpbhousing-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"kpbhousing-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "employees": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Town and school employees, FY2008 to FY2040</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Full-time equivalents. Town departments are budgeted positions from the Town's Financial Plans; school staff are the state's count. The shaded years are the base case forecast.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"employees-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"employees-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 400\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"employees-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"employees-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"employees-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"employees-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "gl-revenue": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Construction permitted, and the taxable value it became</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Top: estimated cost on every building permit for taxable property issued each calendar year (Town permit records; Town schools, fire stations and other tax-exempt property left out). Bottom: the real estate part of the new growth valuation the state certified (business equipment, which needs no building permit, taken out), placed in the fiscal year it was first taxed, July to June. For the two years not yet certified, the bars are what the permits point to at past rates, and the line is what the base case assumes. Each arrow joins a year&rsquo;s permits to the new growth they became. $ millions.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gl-revenue-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"gl-revenue-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 520\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gl-revenue-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gl-revenue-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gl-revenue-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gl-revenue-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "gl-services": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Homes grew; police and fire staffing did not, FY2010 to FY2025</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Each line set to 100 in FY2010. The Census counts every home in 2010 and 2020 (circled); the dashed line between and after is the trend. The purple line is the assessors&rsquo; count on each January 1 from 2016, cleaned of record changes and set to the Census count in 2020. Town positions are budgeted full-time equivalents from the Town&rsquo;s Financial Plans; students and school staff are the state&rsquo;s counts.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gl-services-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"gl-services-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gl-services-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gl-services-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gl-services-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gl-services-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "gl-enroll": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Kindergarten followed births, not new construction</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Brookline kindergartners each fall (state enrollment counts), resident births five years earlier (state birth reports), and new housing units authorized by building permit that year (Census Bureau).</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gl-enroll-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"gl-enroll-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gl-enroll-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gl-enroll-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gl-enroll-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gl-enroll-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "gl-towns": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Towns that added homes gained children, about half as many per home</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Each dot is a Massachusetts city or town with at least 2,000 homes, 2010 to 2020 (Census). The solid line is the fitted relationship; the dashed line is where it would sit if each added home held as many children as an existing one.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gl-towns-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"gl-towns-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 420\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gl-towns-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gl-towns-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gl-towns-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gl-towns-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "gl-sales": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Single-family home sales and kindergartners per birth</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Sales of $100,000 or more recorded on the Town&rsquo;s assessment rolls (left scale), and kindergartners that fall per resident birth five years earlier (right scale). Fall 2020 is the first pandemic year.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gl-sales-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"gl-sales-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gl-sales-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gl-sales-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gl-sales-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gl-sales-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "gl-leads": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>How far ahead each reading looks</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Each row starts when the number is in hand. Dark bars are what it predicts closely; light bars are what it still informs, more loosely.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"gl-leads-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"gl-leads-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n        <div class=\"tooltip\" id=\"gl-leads-tooltip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"gl-leads-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"gl-leads-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"gl-leads-table\"></div>\n    </div>",
 "births-watch": "<div class=\"chart-block\">\n      <div class=\"chart-head\">\n        <h3>Births remain well below what the other two forecasts assume</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Births to Brookline residents each year (state birth reports), and the births each enrollment forecast assumes. Cropper-McKibben, the School Department's forecaster, publishes five-year totals, shown as yearly averages. A year's births set the kindergarten class about five years later.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-svg-wrap\" id=\"births-watch-wrap\">\n        <svg class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"\" id=\"births-watch-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"></svg>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" id=\"births-watch-legend\"></div>\n      <button class=\"toggle-table-btn\" data-target=\"births-watch-table\">Show data table</button>\n      <div class=\"data-table-wrap\" id=\"births-watch-table\"></div>\n    </div>"
}
